{"ts":"2026-08-07T17:13:34.757Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"42d376a0ebc79212ad1dd49b","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"1","source":"environment"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.224","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-07T17:13:34.757Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Another instance of the subcommand-scoped positional requirement, found while measuring graph analytics 2026-08-07. `pm graph dominators --json` exits 2 with \"graph dominators requires an item id\" under code invalid_argument_value. It is a correct refusal and it is invisible from the declared arity: `pm graph --help` renders the id positional as \"Root item id (traversals, paths, impact, and dominators)\", so the requirement is carried in prose inside an argument description rather than in the grammar. Of the sixteen graph subcommands, four require the id positional, one requires a second target positional, and eleven take none, all under a single declared `[id] [target]` shape. This is the same class as the schema/profile/plan versus graph/merge divergence already recorded here: one command, several arities, and the arity a caller must satisfy is discoverable only by being refused."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-07T17:13:34.757Z"}],"before_hash":"d2df3dd35af815bebedf90c26845ee6634e90d284a96372366dd26a765cd2e3c","after_hash":"49a1e018a8c17b1645a2db50b7f405f5fe0720f7a8c86810055877b9c5137032"}
